  "notes": "A compound of {逃|に}げる (to flee) and {避|さ}ける (to avoid). Often used in the compound {現実|げんじつ}{逃避|とうひ} (escapism, escaping from reality), which is one of the most common collocations.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {現実|げんじつ}{逃避|とうひ} (escapism)\n- {責任|せきにん}{逃避|とうひ} (shirking responsibility)\n- {逃避|とうひ}する (to escape, to evade)\n- {逃避|とうひ}{行動|こうどう} (avoidance behavior)\n- {逃避|とうひ}{先|さき} (place of refuge)\n\nUnlike {逃|に}げる, which focuses on the physical act of fleeing, {逃避|とうひ} emphasizes the psychological avoidance of duties, problems, or reality. It often appears in written or formal contexts.",
